Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:45:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FLOWTRACE2: the op-log FLOW line also carries the In Arm pick
 / Tray Arm / Empty cursors, the stack layer counts, InArmSuckUse and the In
 Arm IC bits -- EastSun 1008 'InArmSuckUse[2][4]: its current state' (and
 iLoaderLayerCount_9050 earlier); both lived only in memory.

csystem.cpp W906_FlowTraceTick (end of file): appended ' | pickLd= trayArm= empPick= | layer L= E= A=a1/a2/a3 | suckUse=rrrr/rrrr
  suckIC=rrrr/rrrr' (iPickFromLoadStageTask, CatchTrayTask, iCatchFromEmpty9050Task, iLoader/Empty/Auto1-3LayerCount_9050,
  InArmSuckUse[2][4], InArmSuck.Item != NULL_IC). Still one line per change. Nothing parses FLOW lines (tools/wb_serve.cpp writes them).
tests: test_flow9050_tray.cpp [FT] captures the line and matches the whole tail; Flow9050_Tray 138/138, FP9050_Pure / Index,
  W6_6_CSystemCycle, mainproc_guard passed. Release linked; Debug compiled (wb_serve open: links at EastSun's next F5).
WORKLOG row 204.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 csystem.cpp                  | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/WORKLOG_MACHINE.md      |  1 +
 tests/test_flow9050_tray.cpp | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/csystem.cpp b/csystem.cpp
index 172ca8e..9df9342 100644
--- a/csystem.cpp
+++ b/csystem.cpp
@@ -34077,6 +34077,31 @@ void W906_FlowTraceTick()
                   MOT[MMTrayY].HasIC()?1:0, InArmSuck.HasIC()?1:0, FLCarryKit.HasIC()?1:0, FTestSuck.HasIC()?1:0, FRCarryKit.HasIC()?1:0, OutArmSuck.HasIC()?1:0,
                   LoadTask_9050, iCatchFromLoader9050Task, iArmTask, iInArmPlaceToShuttleTask, AutoSHT1Task, AutoSHT2Task, iTestHeadMotorTask,
                   iTestYFinePitchTask, iTestYFrontTask, iFrontTestSuckICTask, iFrontTestDestroyICTask, OutArmTask, iPickFromShuttle1Task);
+    //AI(W906-FLOWTRACE2) 20261008: EastSun 1008 asked for live values the op log did not carry (iLoaderLayerCount_9050, InArmSuckUse[2][4],
+    //  where the Tray Arm / Empty / In Arm pick stand). Appended at the end of the line (nothing parses FLOW lines; tools/wb_serve.cpp only
+    //  writes them): pickLd = iPickFromLoadStageTask (DoInArmPickFromLoadStage_9045), trayArm = CatchTrayTask (DoCatchTray), empPick =
+    //  iCatchFromEmpty9050Task, layers L(oader) / E(mpty) / A(uto)1-3, suckUse = InArmSuckUse rows (1 = this sucker is used for the pick),
+    //  suckIC = InArmSuck.Item rows (1 = IC data on that sucker).
+    {
+        extern int iPickFromLoadStageTask, CatchTrayTask, iCatchFromEmpty9050Task;
+        char use[2 * (MAX_ARM_Col + 1) + 1] = "", ic[2 * (MAX_ARM_Col + 1) + 1] = "";
+        int k = 0, m = 0;
+        for(int i = 0; i < MAX_ARM_Row; i++)
+        {
+            for(int j = 0; j < MAX_ARM_Col; j++)
+            {
+                use[k++] = InArmSuckUse[i][j] ? '1' : '0';
+                ic[m++]  = (InArmSuck.Item[i][j] != NULL_IC) ? '1' : '0';
+            }
+            if(i + 1 < MAX_ARM_Row) { use[k++] = '/'; ic[m++] = '/'; }
+        }
+        use[k] = 0; ic[m] = 0;
+        const size_t n = std::strlen(b);
+        std::snprintf(b + n, sizeof(b) - n, " | pickLd=%d trayArm=%d empPick=%d | layer L=%d E=%d A=%d/%d/%d | suckUse=%s suckIC=%s",
+                      iPickFromLoadStageTask, CatchTrayTask, iCatchFromEmpty9050Task,
+                      iLoaderLayerCount_9050, iEmptyLayerCount_9050, iAuto1LayerCount_9050, iAuto2LayerCount_9050, iAuto3LayerCount_9050,
+                      use, ic);
+    }
     static std::string s_last;
     if(s_last!=b) { s_last=b; g_W906FlowNote(b); }
 }
